        <div id="testing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            7. Testing Claims and the Fake-Product Problem
          </h2>

          <p>
            Indian retailer listings for Biozyme Performance Whey cite testing by <strong>Informed Choice</strong> in the UK, <strong>Labdoor</strong> in the US and <strong>Trustified</strong> in India, described as checks for label accuracy, including the absence of amino spiking, and for purity. The listings also say batch-wise reports from an NABL-accredited lab are available on the MuscleBlaze website. That is a stronger testing story than most budget brands offer in any country.
          </p>

          <p>
            Read the claims precisely, though. Coverage differs by product: Whey Gold listings cite Labdoor, while the Raw Whey and Beginner's listings we checked did not name a third-party program. If certification matters to you, for example because you compete in a tested sport, search the specific product in the Informed Choice database rather than assuming the whole range is covered.
          </p>

          <p>
            Counterfeit and diverted supplements are a long-standing worry in India's sports nutrition market, which is one reason testing programs and batch reports have become selling points. The safest approach is to buy from the brand's own site or from a large retailer that buys directly, keep the batch number, and compare it with the brand's published report. Unusually low prices from unfamiliar sellers are the clearest warning sign.
          </p>

          <p>
            The same logic applies, more strongly, outside India. An imported tub on a US marketplace has passed through more hands and may have been stored in heat for longer than you would like. Whey is fairly stable, but heat and humidity can affect flavor and mixing, so freshness is a fair concern. Our <a href="/is-protein-powder-safe/">is protein powder safe</a> guide covers what to check on any label.
          </p>
        </div>

