          <p>
            For a rough dollar comparison, 130 to 145 rupees per 25 g of protein works out to around $1.50 to $1.70 at recent exchange rates, which is in the same range as a mid-priced US whey bought in the US. That is the key point for international readers: MuscleBlaze is good value in India, but it is not a bargain once import costs are added, so there is little reason to seek it out abroad.
          </p>

          <p>
            Ignore the printed MRP when comparing. Indian listings often show a maximum retail price with a 10 to 25 percent discount applied, plus extra coupon codes. Compare the price you will actually pay on the day, and compare it on cost per 25 g of protein rather than per jar or per scoop.
