            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per jar</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A 1 kg jar of Biozyme holds about 27 to 28 servings because each scoop is 36 g, while a leaner whey may hold over 30. Comparing price per jar or per kilogram hides that difference. Divide the price by the total grams of protein, then multiply by 25, to compare products fairly.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Beginner's Whey to save money</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Beginner's Whey lists only 12 g of protein per scoop, roughly half a standard serving. It looks cheaper per jar, but you pay for a lot of non-protein powder. For most adults, Biozyme or Raw Whey delivers far more protein per rupee and per scoop.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting unusually cheap sellers</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Counterfeit and diverted supplements are a known problem in India's sports nutrition market. A price far below other major retailers is the clearest warning sign. Buy from the brand site or a large retailer, keep the batch number, and check it against the brand's published lab report.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Importing it into the US</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                MuscleBlaze is good value in India, but import costs remove most of that advantage, and third-party imports add questions about storage and freshness. A US whey such as Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard costs about the same per 25 g and arrives fresher, with a clear return path.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every tub is certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Biozyme listings cite Informed Choice, Labdoor and Trustified, and Whey Gold cites Labdoor, but the Raw Whey and Beginner's listings we checked did not name a program. Tested athletes should look up the exact product in the certifier's database before relying on it.
